Visual check (all 8 inspected with vision): full frames, no scroll chrome,
no captions. V1 run cards label on speaker change only (ASSISTANT once per
run; continuation inside the same card carries no label; USER card tinted);
tool runs icon-compact with counts (terminal ×4 / apply_patch +2 −1); diff
hunks styled (teal +, red −, amber @@) with numbered gutter; code rows wrap
(no mid-word cut at the right edge); emoji (✅ ⚠️ 🚀) render color on both
surfaces. V2 rail: dots per speaker, name at change, timestamps, live tick.
V3 dense: sticky header, role tags at boundaries only, icon one-liners.
Tofu frames: BEFORE rows show the raw PUA glyphs as notdef boxes (the tofu
the app paints today); AFTER rows show [ok]/[warn]/[env] tags with emoji
preserved; mapping table rows wrap cleanly. Board frames end on a card
boundary (no mid-card clip); phone frames end with the final assistant card
visible in full.
